{"h":3395,"lines":[{"t":"Test 2","y":0.10244266582374573,"c":1,"w":0.058264249165852849,"h":0.014591412493702438,"x":0.13136170247342915},{"t":"Questions 27-31","h":0.0165950249446154,"w":0.16310595194498698,"y":0.14487199827966357,"c":1,"x":0.13346392878173977},{"t":"Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","w":0.34567901611328122,"c":1,"x":0.1337448541901147,"y":0.17873969374059062,"h":0.017481236631934793},{"w":0.54129414876302095,"t":"Write the correct letter in boxes 27-31 on your answer sheet.","x":0.13160414981098592,"y":0.21069177015295915,"h":0.017763243406765272,"c":1},{"x":0.12951055797126818,"h":0.021055324900417061,"t":"27 When referring to laughter in the first paragraph, the writer emphasises","y":0.24208981174028166,"c":1,"w":0.67516443888346356},{"x":0.21604938412421404,"h":0.014546867815428799,"t":"its impact on language.","c":1,"w":0.21193415323893228,"y":0.27179034160268056},{"h":0.013081395583944833,"t":"B","w":0.016460905075073223,"c":1,"x":0.17489711939074087,"y":0.28924418583551925},{"t":"C","x":0.17489711937604363,"w":0.016460905075073223,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"y":0.30523255791296955},{"t":"D","x":0.17489711959189586,"w":0.018518517812093099,"y":0.32267441839365896,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944611},{"y":0.28769140178078945,"h":0.014723203769140158,"t":"its function in human culture.","w":0.26131685892740886,"c":1,"x":0.21604938877189228},{"c":1,"h":0.013083107479890721,"y":0.30523255801030136,"t":"its value to scientific research.","x":0.21604938305206209,"w":0.27572016398111976},{"x":0.2139917732592507,"y":0.32122093007947639,"c":1,"w":0.30864196777343755,"t":"its universality in animal societies.","h":0.01598837238037687},{"w":0.53326604207356776,"h":0.019884217333035359,"c":1,"y":0.35258357691161124,"t":"28 What does the writer suggest about Charley Douglass?","x":0.1315521937647737},{"w":0.617283935546875,"y":0.37926972886549148,"c":1,"t":"He understood the importance of enjoying humour in a group setting.","x":0.21399177707117731,"h":0.016195524146054185},{"w":0.6708745320638021,"t":"B He believed that TV viewers at home needed to be told when to laugh.","x":0.17484675149303844,"y":0.39496562626915555,"h":0.016540771659608433,"c":1},{"h":0.018089198953832986,"c":1,"x":0.21392613643139724,"y":0.41162353742268132,"t":"He wanted his shows to appeal to audiences across the social spectrum.","w":0.65240361531575519},{"w":0.016460905075073251,"h":0.013081395583944833,"c":1,"t":"D","x":0.17695473253007066,"y":0.43168604630063556},{"w":0.67499506632486972,"h":0.017861570710989816,"c":1,"x":0.20983098453068208,"t":"He preferred shows where audiences were present in the recording studio.","y":0.42849922219094672},{"c":1,"t":"29 What makes the Santa Cruz study particularly significant?","x":0.13374484789692337,"y":0.46220930216413969,"w":0.55555557250976562,"h":0.016000356213644928},{"c":1,"w":0.48989893595377598,"x":0.21803316497499547,"h":0.017228630883674101,"y":0.48822750848811691,"t":"the various different types of laughter that were studied"},{"t":"the similar results produced by a wide range of cultures","h":0.020054049991746981,"c":1,"y":0.50377355194340268,"x":0.20769550440490112,"w":0.50236658732096351},{"c":1,"y":0.52179034159594606,"t":"the number of different academic disciplines involved","x":0.20781894107924348,"h":0.016000356213644928,"w":0.48353907267252605},{"x":0.1769547325447679,"h":0.011627907185728592,"t":"D","w":0.016460905075073251,"y":0.54069767421721326,"c":1},{"w":0.50430374145507817,"c":1,"y":0.53774459675859498,"h":0.018756682235304356,"t":"the many kinds of people whose laughter was recorded","x":0.20774559752430244},{"x":0.133622031712721,"y":0.56287801728287701,"w":0.55170237223307295,"h":0.019873733655302761,"c":1,"t":"30 Which of the following happened in the San Diego study?"},{"t":"Some participants became very upset.","x":0.22007361100701084,"w":0.34378908793131513,"h":0.017422942306464573,"y":0.59005217654774689,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.6090116276804115,"h":0.013081395583944611,"x":0.17901234548049319,"t":"B","w":0.014403292338053375},{"h":0.013081395583944611,"w":0.018518517812093099,"x":0.17695473276062013,"y":0.62499999975163234,"t":"C","c":1},{"y":0.63517441868157465,"x":0.17901234567919863,"h":0.018895348053517669,"t":"D","w":0.016460905075073223,"c":1},{"t":"Participants exchanged roles.","w":0.26748970031738284,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"x":0.22016461502649379,"y":0.60747938752463926},{"y":0.62279772859847926,"w":0.47338058471679689,"t":"Participants who had not met before became friends.","h":0.016989171013534476,"x":0.22008753730228173,"c":1},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.22016460883307143,"y":0.64098837194268465,"w":0.36213991800944012,"t":"Some participants were unable to laugh.","c":1},{"c":1,"t":"31 In the fifth paragraph, what did the results of the San Diego study suggest?","w":0.71011749267578128,"x":0.13364665832999512,"y":0.67143358386658603,"h":0.021424555244940025},{"y":0.69758539479801451,"x":0.22016461282110014,"t":"It is clear whether a dominant laugh is produced by a high- or low-status","w":0.64197530110677092,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1},{"y":0.73011772055861091,"t":"Low-status individuals in a position of power will still produce submissive","h":0.020772846343239393,"c":1,"x":0.21593857978780251,"w":0.64842671712239586},{"c":1,"y":0.76744186023855099,"w":0.016460905075073223,"x":0.17901234571349217,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"C"},{"c":1,"t":"The submissive laughs of low- and high-status individuals are surprisingly","x":0.20978836829012418,"y":0.76363991807283149,"w":0.66686365763346356,"h":0.019982503075481772},{"t":"D","c":1,"w":0.016460905075073223,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.17901234571349217,"y":0.80087209279669047},{"t":"similar.","y":0.78426150478998791,"x":0.22193971222385178,"w":0.066612275441487623,"c":1,"h":0.013492810010067524},{"x":0.21596987972246875,"w":0.65038192749023438,"c":1,"h":0.020348118668590987,"t":"High-status individuals can always be identified by their way of laughing.","y":0.79668753568225303},{"w":0.026748971939086902,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"x":0.13580246865151277,"t":"46","y":0.9200581393628241}],"w":2400}